M1 (scripts/pickup-watch.mjs passActions, re-arm) The re-arm fires on every pass, forever, for any picked-up idle role whose watchRunning is not true, and a missing field counts as not true. Probe: {role: Manager, state: idle, tokens: 180000, pickedUp: true} gives "arm your dispatch watch" on pass 1, 2 and 3. pickedUp stays true until the next reset, so every idle role the watchdog can't prove has a watch (Manager has none, and an agent can't see a background wake-watch from a thread) gets a message, and a turn, each pass. Fix: read the watch by program inside --pass (for example, look for a running wake-watch.mjs process with that --role), send the re-arm once per pickup at most, and only to roles that use a dispatch watch (the config can name them). Test: three passes over the same row send at most one re-arm; a role with no watch kind gets none.

